Verifier Guide

A guide for task authors preparing verification materials.

Prepare Verification Materials

Upload the following materials to the task card's VERIFICATION section:
Field	Files to provide	Note
Reference files	The ground-truth file for --gt and any additional evaluation references, such as fixed layouts, constraint data, annotations, or reference renders.	Contents, evaluation purpose, and corresponding input argument, if applicable.
Rubrics	A task-specific scoring document (e.g., scoring.md) defining scoring items, criteria, metrics, weights or maximum points, thresholds, total score calculation, and rules for invalid results.	Applicable task and purpose of the rubric.
Scoring scripts	evaluate.py and any required helper scripts, configuration files, and dependency information.	Purpose of the entry point and supporting resources.

Uploaded files are saved under verification/. For each file, complete the Relative path and Note:

    Relative path: Enter a path relative to verification/. For example, evaluate.py is saved as verification/evaluate.py. Preserve required folder structures and avoid duplicate paths.
    Note: Describe the file's contents and evaluation role. Include relevant formats, units, or input arguments.

Click Choose files or Choose a folder, or drag files or a folder into the upload area. Before submitting, check that all required files are included and their paths and notes are correct.
Notes

    Provide complete materials. Include all required references, supporting resources, and dependency information.
    Keep scoring consistent. Ensure that the rubric and scoring scripts use the same criteria, thresholds, weights, and total score calculation.
    Test before submission. Test the complete evaluation, including the handling of invalid or incomplete results.

For requirements on the evaluation entry point, arguments, execution, and score outputs, see the Verifier Template.
Capability Evaluation

When designing the rubric, aim to cover the following four capability areas. Adapt the criteria and weights to the task, and use observable evidence to support each score.
Capability	Evaluation focus
Input Understanding	Understand and follow requirements, interpret references, and identify spatial and object relationships.
Physical Geometry and Structure	Build or reconstruct valid geometry, organize parts, and preserve unaffected regions during edits.
Functionality and Engineering Constraints	Achieve the intended function while satisfying engineering constraints.
Output and Execution	Use permitted tools and resources, deliver valid, traceable outputs, and diagnose and correct errors.

For detailed evaluation criteria, refer to List of evaluation abilities in the shared Feishu knowledge base.
